    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "The most dangerous cost scenario in multi-agent systems is the recursive loop: an agent that enters a cycle of unproductive iterations, consuming tokens with each attempt while making no real progress. These loops emerge from agents trying to self-correct, reasoning through complex problems, or getting stuck in tool-calling patterns that don't resolve. Unlike traditional infinite loops that you catch with timeouts, agent loops are time-bounded but token-unbounded-each iteration takes finite time but consumes significant tokens."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
